---
import { PngComponent } from "../components/png.component";
import Layout from "../layout/Layout.astro";
const title = 'Convert HEIC to PNG Online — Separate Files or Batch ZIP';
const description = 'Convert HEIC photos to separate PNG images in your browser. Download each result or a batch ZIP, with local photo processing and no account.';
const ogImage = "/og-image/heic-to-png.png";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} ogTitle={title}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h1 class="text-center font-bold text-4xl mt-12 mb-5">Convert HEIC to PNG</h1>
    <p class="text-center text-zinc-700 mb-8">Choose PNG when an editor or upload form asks for it. Each selected HEIC becomes a separate PNG; Download All packages those images in a ZIP.</p>
    <PngComponent client:visible />
    <section class="mt-12 mb-10 prose max-w-none" aria-labelledby="conversion-steps">
      <h2 id="conversion-steps">How to convert HEIC to PNG</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose <strong>Choose files</strong> and select the HEIC photos on your device.</li>
        <li>Wait for conversion to finish. It starts automatically after selection.</li>
        <li>Select a finished preview to save that image, or choose Download All for a ZIP of the separate results.</li>
        <li>Check the downloaded result before sharing it. Choose <strong>Convert More</strong> to start another batch.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Selected photo bytes are processed locally in your browser rather than uploaded to a conversion server. The website still loads its scripts and other web resources. No account or conversion fee is required.</p>
      <p>For alternatives and troubleshooting, read the <a href="/blog/heic-to-png/">HEIC to PNG guide</a> and <a href="/how-it-works/">how conversion works</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose max-w-none mb-10" aria-labelledby="conversion-limits">
      <h2 id="conversion-limits">What to check before using the result</h2>
      <p>PNG stores decoded image pixels with lossless compression, but conversion does not preserve every HEIC feature, HDR rendering or metadata field. It does not remove backgrounds or create transparency in an opaque photo. PNG photos can be larger than their HEIC originals.</p>
      <p>Large photos or batches can need substantial memory. If conversion fails, try a single complete HEIC file, then a smaller batch. Support can vary with the HEIC variant, browser and available device memory.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose max-w-none mb-16" aria-labelledby="format-choice">
      <h2 id="format-choice">When to choose PNG</h2>
      <p>PNG is useful when the destination specifically requires it. For an ordinary photo attachment with a small size limit, compare JPG. For a website image, compare WebP. Keep the original HEIC and check the downloaded copy before using it.</p>
      <p>Compare <a href="/blog/heic-jpg-png-pdf-which-format/">JPG, PNG, WebP and PDF</a>, or use the <a href="/blog/heic-photo-upload-not-supported/">photo upload checklist</a> if a form still rejects your file.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
